 ## Overview
-The Contour Tree is a topological data structure that represents the connectivity of level sets (contours) of a scalar field as the isovalue varies [S1, unofficial][S2]. It solves the problem of tracking how contours are created, split, merged, and destroyed by mapping these events to a tree structure where edges correspond to individual contour classes and vertices correspond to critical points [S1, unofficial][S2]. It sets itself apart from the [Reeb Graph](9315-reeb-graph.md) by requiring a simply connected domain without loops, and from the [Topological Landscape](8481-topological-landscape.md) by providing the explicit graph structure rather than just a visual metaphor of peaks and valleys.
